{"reference":"1 Samuel 27","book":"1 Samuel","chapter":27,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Within 1 Samuel","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"First Samuel traces a movement from Eli’s failing priestly house through Samuel’s leadership and Saul’s rejected kingship to David’s anointing, rise, exile, and Saul’s death. David’s stay among the Philistines in this chapter belongs to the book’s portrayal of his exile before Saul’s death.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_samuel_027_732a03c79b7275994cf12e5f"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}